# ==============================================
# GIT LINE-ENDING RULES
# ==============================================
# File Location: Beat-the-Box-Card-Game/.gitattributes
# Status: ACTIVE
# Version: 1.0
# Last Updated: 2026-10-20
#
# VERSION 1.0 CHANGES (2026-10-20):
# - New. Every text file uses LF line endings, on every computer.
#
# DESCRIPTION:
# -----------
# Tells Git how to treat line endings. Windows ends lines with CRLF and
# Linux/Mac use LF; without this file the repo gets a mix, which causes the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings and diffs where every line changed.
#   text=auto  - Git detects which files are text (images stay untouched)
#   eol=lf     - text files are LF in the repo AND in your working folder
#
# NOTES:
# -----
# - After adding this file, run once: git add --renormalize .
# - VS Code and Python handle LF files fine on Windows.

* text=auto eol=lf
